5	 * ~4,000 comets that keeps a full re-propagation of the whole catalogue at
6	 * 60 fps essentially free, and means changing the time is a single uniform
7	 * update rather than 46,000 CPU solves.
8	 *
9	 * Everything is float32, so the element epochs are stored as days from J2000
10	 * (small numbers) rather than raw Julian dates (~2.4e6, which would burn the
11	 * entire mantissa).
